 {"id":"PERF-001","status":"in_progress","priority":"P2","type":null,"complexity":1,"title":"P2 — tests/cli.test.ts pays a ~620ms npx tax on every CLI spawn: 38.90s -> 18.89s (2.06x) by calling the tsx binary directly","reasoning":"MEASUREMENT (2026-11-16, speclang-perf tick speclang-perf-2026-11-16-06-03-30). Hot path: tests/cli.test.ts:125 builds the CLI command with \"npx tsx --tsconfig <cfg> src/cli/index.ts\" and tests/cli.test.ts:127 (cliExec) spawns it once per test. Per-file attribution from a structured vitest run (--reporter=json): tests/cli.test.ts = 49,390ms of 110,577ms cumulative across 101 files (44.7%), the single largest consumer; next is tests/daemon/arch004-autonomous-cascade.test.ts at 15,167ms. PER-SPAWN PROFILE (hyperfine, 2 warmup + 5 runs, same cwd): npx tsx on a trivial file 878.1ms +/- 26.6 vs direct tsx binary 168.3ms +/- 8.0 (5.22x); on the real CLI command (list over 464 specs) npx tsx = 1.062s +/- 0.028 vs direct = 439.4ms +/- 8.7 (2.42x). Mechanism confirmed by exec census (strace -f -c -e trace=execve): npx arm forks 30 execve per invocation, direct arm 4 — the ~620ms delta is npx resolution fan-out, not tsx startup. FILE-LEVEL A/B, same command \"TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run tests/cli.test.ts --reporter=dot\", same pass set (41 passed | 2 skipped): BEFORE 38.90s (tests 38.41s, loadavg 9.20 -> 7.37); AFTER 18.89s (tests 18.39s, loadavg 6.34 -> 6.99) with the patch in worktree /home/kara/speclang-wt-perfcli at HEAD 08b77a59 (node_modules + dist symlinked). The UNPATCHED control was re-run in that SAME worktree and returned 38.90s (38.41s tests), so the 20.01s delta (-51.4%) is the patch, not the worktree. SUITE LEVEL: main tree 39.22s / 1826 passed | 58 skipped vs patched worktree 19.81s at matched loadavg (7-9). CAVEAT: the patched arm resolved tsx through SPECLANG_TSX_BIN because the shared node_modules has no local tsx, which is itself part of the defect — today the spawn depends on whatever tsx npx resolves (on this host PATH tsx is /home/kara/.hermes/hermes-agent/node_modules/.bin/tsx, a foreign install). FIX (one change, two files): (a) package.json devDependencies add \"tsx\": \"4.23.15\" (the version the npx cache currently resolves) and install so node_modules/.bin/tsx exists; (b) tests/cli.test.ts:125 resolve TSX_BIN = path.join(REPO_ROOT, \"node_modules\", \".bin\", \"tsx\") and build the CLI string from it instead of \"npx tsx\". No test expectation and no CLI source change is needed.","acceptance_criteria":"From /home/kara/speclang: (1) tests/cli.test.ts no longer shells out through npx for the CLI runner — the runner line resolves node_modules/.bin/tsx; \"jq -r .devDependencies.tsx package.json\" prints a non-null pin and \"ls node_modules/.bin/tsx\" succeeds after install. (2) Re-run the SAME measured command \"TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run tests/cli.test.ts --reporter=dot\" on an idle box: 41 passed | 2 skipped (43) and Duration at or below 22s (pre-row baseline 38.90s, patched arm 18.89s). (3) Whole-suite check \"TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp npx vitest run --reporter=dot\" keeps 1826 passed | 58 skipped (1884) and Duration at or below 30s (baseline 39.22s). Paste both Duration lines into the closing note. Do not alter tests/cli.test.ts expectations, timeouts, or src/cli in this row.","detail":{"fingerprint":"4238ad897c8fe9c0d31941918fe677f5f0b4be35afa79b64bf354436f1d8898b"},"capability_tags":["performance","tests"],"created_at":"2026-11-16T06:30:09.768555+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-16T22:49:44.568076+00:00","worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/speclang-PERF-001","branch":"wt/PERF-001","sessions":["speclang-perf-2026-11-16-22-47-48"]}
