 {"id":"QA-SPECLANG-007","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"bug","complexity":2,"title":"[P1] QA rig grades lint/build against an npm ci --ignore-scripts install, so a repo whose lint depends on its own postinstall is reported FAIL","reasoning":"speclang-qa-2026-11-16-06-03-37 cell=fresh-install+lint. bunker-qa.sh hardcodes 'npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund' (scripts/bunker-qa.sh:857-860) for the install/tests/lint path, so any repo whose lint or build depends on its own postinstall hook is graded FAIL for a defect a normal user install never hits. Proven on speclang at canonical tip d4e69294 in a fresh clone (/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/speclang-verify-2026-11-16-06-03-37/fresh): plain 'npm ci --no-audit --no-fund' then 'npm run lint' exits 0 (3 warnings) because scripts/postinstall-lint-deps.sh stages the TS6 alias for typescript-eslint; the battery's identical lint cell exited rc=2 with 'typescript-eslint does not support TS 7.0'. The same --ignore-scripts install also strips native install scripts (better-sqlite3 prebuild), which muddies the tests cell. Battery evidence: /home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/speclang-qa-2026-11-16-06-03-37/harvest/qa-evidence.jsonl, SHA256 b516fb98a6307c3ea14c813862b7c12896fb5c0e68427049c5716a29e00f6604, 24 rows / 15 distinct cells (FAIL=5, INFO=2, N/A=6, OK=11), agent-head 596cc628 (not resolvable in the canonical object DB, so source currency stays UNVERIFIED).","acceptance_criteria":"bunker-qa.sh must stop grading lint/build/tests cells against an install that silently skipped the repo's own install scripts without recording the condition: either install with scripts enabled for repos that declare a postinstall entry, or mark the dependent cells UNVERIFIED/harness-conditioned with the --ignore-scripts caveat in their detail. Verify by re-running the speclang battery on a clean agent: the lint cell must either PASS or be reported harness-skipped naming 'npm ci --ignore-scripts', and the evidence detail must